1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,178
A lead is a prospect you have not qualified yet.

2
00:00:04,178 --> 00:00:08,063
This video shows how to find and add leads, import a list of

3
00:00:08,063 --> 00:00:14,420
them, call and text them, and convert the ones that qualify into contacts, accounts and opportunities.

4
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:23,721
A purchased list or a trade-show scan is full of people who may never buy.

5
00:00:23,721 --> 00:00:28,070
If they were contacts, your customer list would fill with strangers.

6
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:32,018
Leads are kept apart, but you work them the same way:

7
00:00:32,018 --> 00:00:36,028
you can call them, text them, load them as activities and retry them

8
00:00:36,028 --> 00:00:37,600
through a subject flow.

9
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:41,234
When a lead qualifies, you convert it.

10
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:45,430
The lead becomes a contact, and its history moves with it.

11
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:52,402
Open Interaction Center, Leads.

12
00:00:52,402 --> 00:00:59,556
The list shows the open leads, with each lead's status, rating, company, source and list.

13
00:01:00,043 --> 00:01:01,771
Search with terms.

14
00:01:01,771 --> 00:01:07,029
Lead status finds a status by name, Source finds a lead source, and

15
00:01:07,029 --> 00:01:10,126
Rating finds hot, warm or cold leads.

16
00:01:10,126 --> 00:01:13,943
Here, Rating hot shows the leads to call first.

17
00:01:14,436 --> 00:01:18,215
Other terms are List for the list a lead came in, Owner for

18
00:01:18,215 --> 00:01:20,658
the user responsible, and Converted.

19
00:01:20,658 --> 00:01:24,496
The phone search terms from the contacts list work here too.

20
00:01:28,721 --> 00:01:30,152
Click New Lead.

21
00:01:30,152 --> 00:01:35,125
Besides the name and the contact methods, a lead has a Lead status,

22
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:39,621
a Company, a Lead source, a List, a Rating and a Lead owner.

23
00:01:43,864 --> 00:01:46,199
New leads get the default status.

24
00:01:46,199 --> 00:01:51,467
Pick the source from your lead sources, give the list a name, and choose a rating.

25
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:52,604
Then publish.

26
00:01:56,904 --> 00:02:00,859
To load a list, open Content, Import and choose Lead.

27
00:02:00,859 --> 00:02:05,685
The Columns Requirements table shows the columns a file can carry:

28
00:02:05,685 --> 00:02:12,454
the lead status, source, list, company, rating and owner, next to the name and contact methods.

29
00:02:12,934 --> 00:02:17,348
Skip numbers that already belong to a contact leaves out rows whose number

30
00:02:17,348 --> 00:02:20,825
a contact has, so a customer is not called as a stranger.

31
00:02:20,825 --> 00:02:24,797
Skip numbers that already belong to an open lead does the same for

32
00:02:24,797 --> 00:02:26,674
leads you are still working.

33
00:02:26,674 --> 00:02:28,274
Both are on by default.

34
00:02:28,795 --> 00:02:33,524
List name, Lead source, Lead status and Lead owner are given to every

35
00:02:33,524 --> 00:02:36,425
new lead whose row does not set its own.

36
00:02:40,725 --> 00:02:44,167
Everything you do with a contact works on a lead.

37
00:02:44,167 --> 00:02:48,235
Open a lead, and use List Activities to see its activities.

38
00:02:48,729 --> 00:02:55,277
Add Activity, Outbound, schedules a call or a text, and Inbound logs one the lead started.

39
00:02:55,277 --> 00:03:01,689
Leads can also be loaded as activities, and retried by a subject flow, like any contact.

40
00:03:05,905 --> 00:03:09,148
When a lead qualifies, click Convert on its row.

41
00:03:09,148 --> 00:03:13,652
The page says that a contact already has this lead's email, and Merge

42
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:16,415
into is picked, so no duplicate is made.

43
00:03:16,889 --> 00:03:21,914
The contact keeps its own values and only gains what the lead has that it lacks.

44
00:03:21,914 --> 00:03:27,349
The account starts from the lead's company, and Create an opportunity records the deal.

45
00:03:27,803 --> 00:03:33,927
Under Activities, choose to move the open activities to the contact, or to cancel them.

46
00:03:33,927 --> 00:03:35,243
Click Convert.

47
00:03:37,931 --> 00:03:42,287
For a lead nobody knows yet, choose Create a new contact and its

48
00:03:42,287 --> 00:03:46,207
type, create the account, and tick Create an opportunity.

49
00:03:46,207 --> 00:03:51,061
Pick the opportunity type, and enter a name, an amount and a close date.

50
00:03:52,276 --> 00:03:56,296
The lead takes the Converted status and becomes read-only.

51
00:03:56,296 --> 00:04:00,316
It leaves the Leads list, and the contact has its history.

52
00:04:04,516 --> 00:04:08,549
A subject flow can convert a lead when an activity ends with a

53
00:04:08,549 --> 00:04:11,396
chosen disposition, for example Qualified.

54
00:04:11,396 --> 00:04:16,378
Its Convert Lead action runs before the other actions, so a follow-up activity

55
00:04:16,378 --> 00:04:18,216
lands on the new contact.

56
00:04:18,966 --> 00:04:23,562
On an Automatic activity load of a lead type, the AI lead conversion

57
00:04:23,562 --> 00:04:28,903
card lets the AI convert a lead that qualified during an automated call or text.

58
00:04:28,903 --> 00:04:33,436
It never converts a lead who declined or asked not to be contacted.

59
00:04:34,186 --> 00:04:39,286
With Workflows on, a Lead Converted event starts a workflow when any conversion

60
00:04:39,286 --> 00:04:43,546
happens, and a Convert Lead task converts a lead from a workflow.

61
00:04:44,296 --> 00:04:46,907
Three CRM reports follow the leads:

62
00:04:46,907 --> 00:04:52,766
the Lead funnel, the Lead conversion by source and list, and the Opportunity pipeline.

63
00:04:56,966 --> 00:05:01,116
Work a purchased list without polluting the contact list.

64
00:05:01,866 --> 00:05:06,786
Follow trade-show leads through statuses, and call the hot ones first.

65
00:05:07,536 --> 00:05:13,676
Convert a qualified lead into a contact, an account and a deal in one step.

66
00:05:14,426 --> 00:05:20,016
Let the AI qualify leads by text or call, and convert the ones that qualify.

67
00:05:22,016 --> 00:05:26,915
Keep prospects as leads, work them like contacts, and convert the ones that

68
00:05:26,915 --> 00:05:30,664
qualify, so your contact list holds only real customers.

69
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:32,236
Thanks for watching.

